this is the first time zebenesa has  returned to her home  since she and her family fled for their  lives  it is completely destroyed  zebenisa is kyrgyz she has lived in the  village of cocktash  on the disputed border with tajikistan  all her life  there have been clashes between the  kyrgyz and tajik communities  in this region before but never has  military involvement left destruction on  this scale  i had hope that when i came back there  would be something left  but i'm devastated god willing with help  of the people we will rebuild our lives  instead of moving i want to rebuild here  this place has always been home i will  never leave  both the kyrgyz and tajik governments  accuse each other of escalating the  situation  videos shot on mobile phones show the  tajik military moving into disputed  villages  no tajik homes were destroyed in the  attacks  in this village this is one of 17 homes  in this particular village that has been  destroyed and people have begun to come  back  to inspect the damage or in this case  what remains  of their properties and one thing they  all tell you is that there was no  animosity in the community  during the period of the soviets  problems  started with the breakup of the soviet  union independence  and a border problem that has lasted 30  years  the violence was sparked by arguments  between local kyrgyz and tajik residents  over control of water from this  reservoir  kyrgyzstan says tajik soldiers killed  more than 50 people  destroyed government and private  property  inspects the damage to his home  we are afraid my family and children  can't live here  my tajik neighbors were also evacuated  but into their territory  the relationship between us has not been  good for years but now it's worse than  ever  some of the estimated 60 000 people who  were evacuated are sheltering in schools  i've been here with my sister-in-law and  grandchildren for four days  i don't know what's happening in my  village thank god we are being looked  after here  with little sign of a comprehensive  settlement to this complicated border  dispute  zebenesa and many like her will struggle  to rebuild their lives charles stratford  al jazeera  coqtash on the kirigis tajik border
 

